# Jarvis Phase 1 — Walkthrough

## Summary

Built a fully wired, dual-mode (text + voice) local AI assistant. All components tested individually and integrated into the orchestrator.

---

## What Was Built

### Core Pipeline (Text Mode)
- **Orchestrator** → LLM Client → ReAct Agent → 7 System Tools → Mem0 Memory
- Prompt-based tool calling (works with ANY model, no native API needed)
- Run: `python -m jarvis`

### Voice Pipeline (Voice Mode)
- **Wake Word** → **Record** → **STT** → Agent → **TTS** → Speaker
- Run: `python -m jarvis --voice`

---

## Key Files Changed/Created

| File | What |
|---|---|
| [core/orchestrator.py](file:///d:/Jarvis/jarvis/core/orchestrator.py) | Dual text/voice mode, full service wiring |
| [agent/react_agent.py](file:///d:/Jarvis/jarvis/agent/react_agent.py) | Prompt-based ReAct loop (GGUF compatible) |
| [voice/implementations.py](file:///d:/Jarvis/jarvis/voice/implementations.py) | KokoroTTS, WhisperSTT, OpenWakeWordEngine |
| [__main__.py](file:///d:/Jarvis/jarvis/__main__.py) | Added `--voice` and `--config` CLI flags |

---

## Issues Resolved

1. **Nemotron GGUF doesn't support Ollama's native tool API** → Rewrote ReAct agent to use prompt-based JSON tool calling
2. **`tflite-runtime` not available on Windows pip** → Switched OpenWakeWord to ONNX inference framework
3. **OpenWakeWord models not bundled** → Used `openwakeword.utils.download_models()` to fetch them
4. **Mem0 required [ollama](file:///d:/Jarvis/jarvis/agent/tool_registry.py#28-38) Python package** → Installed automatically during test

